<title>SWEDEN: Saab Auto elects board members.</title>
<headline>Saab Auto elects board members.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saab Automobile, jointly owned by U.S. carmaker General Motors and Swedish investment group Investor, said on Friday it appointed David Herman to represent GM on its board.</p>
<p>Saab also said in a statement it elected Robert Hendry, president and CEO of Saab Automobile, as a director.</p>
<p>It added that Peter Wallenberg Jr would succeed board member Marcus Wallenberg, representing Investor. Michael Treschow was the board's new vice chairman, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paul de Bendern, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
